
wildcards are special characters used by the shell to match filenames and paths. They are also called globbing patterns.


| Wildcard        | Meaning                                | Example         |
| --------------- | -------------------------------------- | --------------- |
| `*`             | Matches zero or more characters        | `*.txt`         |
| `?`             | Matches exactly one character          | `file?.txt`     |
| `[ ]`           | Matches one character from a set/range | `file[123].txt` |
| `[! ]` / `[^ ]` | Matches one character NOT in the set   | `file[!0].txt`  |
